d a Magnesium Supplement Label) Tj T* () Tj T* (The difference between buying wisely and buying blindly.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Stand in front of a shelf of supplements for five minutes and you will quickly notice some) Tj T* (thing. Nearly every bottle claims to be:) Tj T* () Tj T* (High strength) Tj T* () Tj T* (Maximum absorption) Tj T* () Tj T* (Premium quality) Tj T* () Tj T* (Pharmaceutical grade) Tj T* () Tj T* (Professional formula) Tj T* () Tj T* (Superior bio availability) Tj T* () Tj T* (The problem is that many of these phrases have no standard scientific definition. A beauti) Tj T* (ful label does not guarantee a better supplement. Learning to read the information panel o) Tj T* (n the back of the bottle is far more valuable than reading the promises on the front.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Front of the Bottle Sells) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Back of the Bottle Explains Think of the front label as advertising. Think of the Supp) Tj T* (lement Facts panel as evidence. Always spend more time reading the back.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Step One) Tj T* () Tj T* (Find the Supplement Facts Panel) Tj T* () Tj T* (Every reputable supplement should clearly display a Supplement Facts panel \(or the equival) Tj T* (ent nutritional information panel required in your country\).) Tj T* () Tj T* (This is where you?ll find:) Tj T* () Tj T* (Serving size) Tj T* () Tj T* (Amount per serving) Tj T* () Tj T* (Elemental magnesium) Tj T* () Tj T* (Other ingredients) Tj T* () Tj T* (Suggested use) Tj T* () Tj T* (Ignore the marketing until you?ve read this panel.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Step Two) Tj T* () Tj T* (Look for Elemental Magnesium) Tj T* () Tj T* (This is one of the biggest mistakes people make. Imagine two products.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Product A) Tj T* () Tj T* (Magnesium Citrate) Tj T* () Tj T* (500 mg) Tj T* () Tj T* (Product B) Tj T* () Tj T* (Magnesium Glycinate) Tj T* () Tj T* (200 mg) Tj T* () Tj T* (At first glance, Product A appears stronger. But appearances can be misleading. The number) Tj T